  "result": "Perfect! All 129 tests pass. Here's what I implemented:\n\n**Changes to src/invoices.js:**\n- Added `lineVat(line)` function that:\n  - Calculates VAT on line amount after discount: (lineTotal - lineDiscount) \u00d7 vatRate / 100\n  - Rounds fractional cents using roundCents()\n  - Clamps result to \u22650\n- Updated `invoiceTotals(invoice)` to return `{ subtotal, discount, vat, total }`\n  - `vat` = sum of all line VATs (each calculated and rounded independently)\n  - `total` = subtotal - discount + vat (clamped to \u22650)\n\n**Changes to src/render.js:**\n- Imported `invoiceTotals` to calculate totals\n- Added VAT display line showing `VAT: \u20acX.XX` (only when VAT > 0)\n- VAT line appears just above the Total line\n- Total line now reflects the calculated total including VAT\n\n**Tests added:**\n- 15 lineVat tests covering:\n  - VAT calculation on full amount and after discount\n  - Different VAT rates (0%, 9%, 21%)\n  - Rounding of fractional cents\n  - Clamping to zero\n- 5 invoiceTotals tests with VAT:\n  - Single line with VAT\n  - Discount + VAT interaction\n  - Multiple lines with different VAT rates\n  - Mixed scenarios\n- 5 renderInvoiceText tests:\n  - VAT line display when VAT > 0\n  - No VAT line when VAT = 0\n  - VAT appears before Total\n  - Correct total calculations including VAT\n  - Mixed VAT rates\n\nAll 129 tests pass. Ready for the next request!",
